items.what:
RELEASE.md:55 now says:
- main's ruleset requires *Web Wallet required* with no bypass, so it refuses a commit pushed to main straight;
- the version reaches main by a PR whose branch carries the sed and cargo update changes and their commit, as 0.7.0's did (cli/0.7.0, 283af4e1, merged as #376, cda19571, which 0.7.0's tag is on) and as 0.8.0's PR set it;
- once that PR is merged, the command run on main as GitHub has it changes nothing, commits nothing, pushes nothing, and its tag starts the release;
- with a version commit to push (the PR not merged yet, or a stale main without the version), it makes the commit, main refuses the push, the next lines still tag that commit and push the tag, and release.yml builds a commit main doesn't hold;
- on a stale main that has the version, the tag goes on an older commit;
- either way, delete the tag and draft (Re-releasing Tag) and start again.
The block itself is unchanged. I checked release.yml: it triggers on any pushed `*.*.*` tag and has no check of where the commit sits.
